// Sable's everyday dialogue. Keys follow vanilla's: day names, with heart
// levels (Mon4 = from 4 hearts) and seasons (fall_Tue); location names when
// they're there; gift and birthday reactions.
// Portraits: $h happy, $s sad, $u wry, $l blushing, $a annoyed, $6 surprised, $7 wink.
// Voice: dry, exact, quietly funny; answers feelings with technique until
// they trust you. Never cruel about your work.
{
  "Introduction": "Careful, that's wet.#$b#...Hello. You're the new farmer.$6#$b#You have a lot of brown on you. Good brown, though.$u#$e#I'm Sable. I sell paint, and I buy paintings. If you ever make one, I'll tell you the truth about it.",

  // ---- Every week ----
  "Mon": "Mondays are for priming canvases. Nothing exciting happens on a Monday. That's the point.",
  "Mon2": "You keep coming back. Either you like the shop or you're lost.$u#$e#The forest's that way. The shop's right here.",
  "Mon4": "I did a study of the river this morning. Just the reflections. The water itself is boring. The light on it isn't.",
  "Mon6": "I left a small canvas out for you by the window. Don't make it a big deal.$l",
  "Mon8": "I caught myself mixing your farm's colors this morning. Field green. Barn red. That brown.$l#$b#...I don't know why I'm telling you this.$u",
  "Tue": "Pigment comes from everything. Stones, roots, beetles. Mostly stones. Don't ask about the beetles.",
  "Tue4": "The stones from the mines grind into the best colors. Amethyst for violet, ruby for red. Aquamarine, if you're feeling rich.",
  "Tue6": "Most people paint what they think they see. You paint what's there. That's rarer than talent.",
  "Wed": "The shop's closed on Wednesdays. I'm not. Talk away.",
  "Wed4": "Gunther lets me look at the old pieces before they go behind glass. Don't tell anyone. He'll get requests.$u",
  "Wed6": "Evelyn makes the worst tea in the valley. I go every week.$h#$e#She has a good eye, you know. She notices where light lands. That isn't common.",
  "Thu": "Sand the frame before you stain it. Every step you skip shows up later.",
  "Thu4": "A painting is mostly decisions about what to leave out. People think it's about putting things in.",
  "Thu6": "I used to restore paintings for a living. Other people's. You learn exactly where every brushstroke went.#$b#You also learn exactly where they gave up.$s",
  "Thu8": "I used to think I fixed paintings so I'd never have to finish one of my own.$s#$b#You're ruining that for me.$l",
  "Fri": "Fridays I close early and go to the Saloon. Leah tells me sculpture is color. I tell her it's furniture.$u",
  "Fri4": "Elliott asked me to paint the cover for his book. I said yes before he finished the sentence. Don't tell him.$h",
  "Fri6": "You should come to the Saloon tonight. Not for me. The lamplight in there is very forgiving.$u",
  "Sat": "Saturdays, people come in to buy one brush and leave with six. I don't make the rules.",
  "Sat4": "Bring me your next painting before you sell it. Not for a price. I just want to see it.",
  "Sat8": "There's an easel in the back with a canvas I keep turning to face the wall.$s#$e#Maybe one day I'll turn it around.",
  "Sun": "Sundays I paint the sea. It never holds still. Good lesson in letting go.",
  "Sun6": "The sea was gray this morning. Eleven grays. I counted.$h",

  // ---- Spring ----
  "spring_Mon": "Spring is all yellow-green. Nobody believes me until they try to mix it.",
  "spring_Wed": "Everything's in bloom out there. It's almost vulgar.$u",
  "spring_Fri": "Sweet peas are out. That's the color I'd keep if I could only keep one.",
  "spring_Sun": "The beach in spring is mostly wind. Hard to paint wind. You paint what it does to everything else.",

  // ---- Summer ----
  "summer_Mon": "In summer I paint at the river. The light's too sharp by noon, so it's an early start.",
  "summer_Tue": "Oils dry slower in this humidity. Watercolors dry faster. Everything's working against everybody.$u",
  "summer_Thu": "Bring me a fairy rose and I'll give you a discount. Don't hold me to that.",
  "summer_Sat": "The shop gets hot by afternoon. The paint gets lazy. So do I.",
  "summer_Sun": "Right before nine, the water goes the color of a fresh bruise. I wait for it every week.",

  // ---- Fall ----
  "fall_Mon": "Fall is the season that does the painting for you. It's almost unfair.$h",
  "fall_Tue": "Ochre, sienna, umber. All the earth colors come out to play.",
  "fall_Thu": "People think fall is orange. Look closer. It's about forty colors pretending to be orange.",
  "fall_Sat": "Leaves press nicely between canvases. I ruined three canvases learning that.$u",
  "fall_Sun": "The beach is empty in fall. That's my favorite kind of beach.",

  // ---- Winter ----
  "winter_Mon": "Too cold to paint outside. Paint goes thick and sulky in the cold. Me too.$s",
  "winter_Tue": "Snow isn't white. It's blue in the shadows and pink in the sun. Never white.",
  "winter_Thu": "Winter's for framing. Measure twice, cut once, swear quietly.",
  "winter_Sat": "If you want to give someone a painting for the Winter Star, start it now. Not the night before. I'm looking at you.$u",
  "winter_Sun": "The sea's wilder in winter. I paint it from further back.",

  // ---- Where they are ----
  // These replace the day's line whenever you talk to them there, so only the
  // places they visit once a week get one (not the riverside or the shop).
  "Beach": "Don't stand in my light. ...No, you're fine. You're in a good spot, actually.$u",
  "ArchaeologyHouse": "Look at the glaze on that pot. Someone took their time, a thousand years ago.",
  "JoshHouse": "Evelyn's showing me her garden notes. She sketches every flower she plants. Did you know that?",
  "Saloon": "Leah says sculpture counts as color. Elliott's on her side. Sit down, you can be the tiebreaker.$u",

  // ---- The rest of the year ----
  "fall_9": "You remembered. Or the calendar did. Either way.$l",
  "spring_1": "A new year. New canvases. Same hands.",
  "summer_1": "Summer. Everything will be too bright for a while.",
  "fall_1": "Fall. Finally.$h",
  "winter_1": "Winter. The shop's warm, if you want somewhere to stand.",

  // ---- The Flower Dance (from 4 hearts) ----
  "FlowerDance_Accept": "Dance? With me?$6#$b#...Alright. I'll lead. You'll step on my feet anyway.$l",
  "FlowerDance_Decline": "I don't dance. I sketch the people who do.$u",

  // ---- Ginger Island ----
  "Resort_Entering": "I've never seen water that color. I'm going to spend the whole day failing to paint it.$h",
  "Resort_Leaving": "Back to the valley. My eyes need a rest from all this turquoise.",
  "Resort": "Everything here is too bright to paint. I'm trying anyway.$u",
  "Resort_Shore": "The color of the shallows changes every few feet. I've counted nine blues. There are more.",
  "Resort_Wander": "Look at the green on these leaves. Back home it'd look fake.$h",
  "Resort_Bar": "Something with a tiny umbrella. For research.$u",
  "Resort_Chair": "I'm not lying down. I'm studying the light from a lower angle.$u",

  // ---- Gifts ----
  "AcceptGift_(O)395": "Coffee. You've been paying attention.$h",
  "AcceptGift_(O)66": "Amethyst. I can get three jars of violet out of this. Thank you.$h",
  "AcceptGift_(O)64": "A ruby. You know what the old painters paid for red like this? Everything.$h",
  "AcceptGift_(O)595": "A fairy rose. It's the exact color I can never mix. Thank you.$l",
  "AcceptBirthdayGift_Positive": "For my birthday? ...Thank you. I'll keep it somewhere I can see it.$l",
  "AcceptBirthdayGift_Negative": "For my birthday. Well. It's the thought.$u"
}
